Contract and acceptance Record; original stage label **15** is retained only for requirement/task/workflow IDs. [Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) is the execution authority.

Contributing packages: [Complete core workspace acceptance](../features/Core-Acceptance.lingua)

## Scheduling interpretation

The linked packages own implementation and its task order. This Record preserves the full source requirements, interface details, examples, research, milestones, fixtures, failure cases and completion evidence. Its `#requires` edges mean all contributors are needed to close this whole contract, not that every consumer waits for this join. Former references to earlier/later stages, delivery cycles or deferred tails describe the appropriate capability subset and composed proofs; they do not restore the removed global sequence. Incomplete unrelated siblings are not regression failures. All already verified affected capabilities must continue working.

For a mixed milestone, each contributor records its verified subset, then this join runs the actual composed workflow when all contributors exist. Do not mark the full milestone done from a local helper or silently drop geographic/hosted/numerical portions. Published exports remain usable without reopening their implementation solely to await this join; fixes to real interface defects remain mandatory.


Finish with the useful local/offline/hosted modeling workspace working as a whole before any new physical-material or scientific capability is scheduled. Completion requires observed user workflows and measured recovery/resource behavior, including the intended scale journey and authored landmarks.

## Required workflow milestones

- [ ] **15.M01.** From the ball in a saved place, travel outward to coarse globe/optional outer context and back; explicitly switch Orbit/Fly/Walk, walk the street with supported optional character/avatar presence, recognize the authored castle, find several favorite-place models in the overview, enter the building and use a mounted Sand.

- [ ] **15.M02.** Edit/simplify/reimport the authored place, batch-edit selected matching objects and modify an exact CAD part. Preserve dimensions, stable IDs, undo/reload, protected openings and authored-versus-source/physical calibration.

- [ ] **15.M03.** Repeat meaningful navigation/editing with an identified editor and restricted public visitor, a separately authenticated Organ source, cold/warm/offline data, caps/denials, slow transfer and host restart. Recover receipts/drafts without stale mutation replay or hidden authority changes.

- [ ] **15.M04.** Use an independent microscopic structure editor and the operational/civic workflow without loading a world or new solver. Existing Areas, gravity, motion cooling and support still work and idle work settles.

- [ ] **15.M05.** Pass the agreed mixed-workload budgets on named hardware or obtain an explicitly reviewed measured profile change. Leave no blocker in claimed core scope; absent deferred heating/material/dynamics features are neither advertised nor prerequisites.

- [ ] **15.M06.** Complete a delegated Fiote edit/authoring task, continue editing its actual result through native tools, focus the same spatial content into a readable flat/HUD view and refresh/reconcile model-linked work under the earlier stage contracts. Cancel or disconnect the provider and keep ordinary scene/navigation/Record controls usable. Complete the software workflow with no extra device, learned scene generator or research-model integration.

- [ ] **15.M07.** Customize a dressed character, pose it with shared articulated tools, inspect the optional detailed anatomical subset and attach a region/pose-pair observation. Let Fiote query/highlight permitted named structures, continue natively, return to a simplified third-person body, walk through the authored building and reopen the detail offline. Retain identity, motion limits, source/annotation privacy and undo while unused internal geometry releases. Repeat basic articulation on the nonhuman/mechanism source; no physical muscle/cloth/hair model or clinical diagnosis is needed.

- [ ] **15.M08.** Complete B42/B43 together: author and inspect a connected PCB, use its functional device in the mixed lamp/camera/actuator scene, switch supported functional models and unload internal geometry. Preserve external behavior, source/model validity, native controls, local overrides, offline closure and authoritative hosted state. Numerical circuit solving remains deferred to 15a.

## Entry and scope

- [ ] Follow the development graph and owned-package delivery rules. Preserve every requirement, composed workflow and evidence obligation below; former stage numbers are stable traceability labels.

- [ ] This is a contract acceptance join. Wait for its explicitly linked contributing packages to pass; there is no previous-numbered-stage implementation prerequisite.

- [ ] Recover the actual contributing package handoffs and open only needed contract sections. Read-only references to other contracts are not additional hard prerequisites.

- [ ] Limit implementation to the current core subset: preserve existing Areas/gravity/motion cooling and implement needed geometry/navigation/definition/hosting contracts. Keep new property evaluation, heating/thermodynamics, additional physical solvers, experiments and calculated-state recording deferred to [stage 15a and stages 16–21](../Workspace-Development.lingua#numerical-scope-and-independent-scientific-readiness). A future example/field/reference below does not activate its evaluator or make it a core exit requirement.

- [ ] Keep one model/accepted-edit/query/artifact/demand implementation. Treat the following source ownership as a starting location to re-audit, not permission to create every proposed crate/profile upfront: `crates/xtask/`; `crates/interface/src/native/`; `crates/engine/src/`; `crates/transport/`; `stage-owned contract modules`.

