## Delivery cycles and retained workflows

- [ ] **Cycle A — Verify retained capabilities individually.** Recover stages 01–14 handoffs and runnable workflow links, then replay the affected core journey, authoring/CAD/structure, operational and articulated subsets on the selected fixture/profile. Record missing coverage and regressions against their original owning requirements.

- [ ] **Cycle B — Compose the real mixed experience.** Combine navigation/authoring, mounted content, offline/hosted delivery, Agent work, operations and B41 detail/cheap-body transitions under aggregate admission. Measure actual contention and failure/recovery; isolated passing results alone cannot establish mixed usability.

- [ ] **Cycle C — Repair at the earliest owning stage and close.** Fix observed defects through their source contracts, rerun the decisive affected checks and repeat mixed runs only when changed behavior or unresolved evidence justifies it. Finalize current handoffs, measured limits and the deferred capability matrix before enabling any numerical expansion.

- [ ] Preserve these contracts; stage 15 integrates previously delivered built-in capabilities and example recipes. It does not add a new framework or weaken an earlier gate to finish stabilization.

