## Concrete acceptance replay

- [ ] **15.P01 — Audit capability coverage before mixed runs; 15.T01/15.T04 / 15.W01–15.W05.** Build the gate matrix from the retained 01–14 workflow paragraphs and their real proof links. For each original milestone identify the current implementation, adopted hard/soft conditions, changed dependencies, latest valid evidence and any missing/regressed behavior. Replay affected proofs and reuse unchanged evidence with its validity boundary; a table row, new screenshot or passing adapter check supplies no missing native outcome. Keep deferred scope separate and every core gap at its earliest owning task.

- [ ] **15.P02 — Execute the complete composed experience; 15.T01–15.T03/15.T05/15.T06 / 15.W01–15.W05.** On the named profile perform the ball/landmark/interior route, authored edit/simplify/reimport/CAD change, optional character detail/cheap-body transition, Fiote/native/HUD continuation and model-linked-work refresh beside real structural and operational use. Add editor/visitor, independent source login, slow transfer/cap/revoke and host restart; repeat the independent non-geographic root. Record a trace showing which tasks overlap. Review navigation, shape, readable input, scope, privacy and recovery as one experience rather than accepting isolated screenshots.

- [ ] **15.P03 — Close the gate with current results; 15.T03/15.T04 / 15.W01–15.W05.** Compare mixed frame/input/commit/query/open percentiles, cold/warm/offline conditions, steady/transient RAM/GPU/disk/queues and cancellation/release with the original profiles and actual workload sizes. Compare repeated travel and settled idle with 01.W01, and assert exact quantities, IDs, rights, receipt recovery and zero unintended worker/network/action starts. Repair failures at their owning stages and rerun only the invalidated proofs plus affected composition. Keep the gate open for unresolved hard or qualitative failures; no budget/scope change is implicit in summary compression.

- [ ] **15.P04 / 15.W06 — Stabilize mixed functional devices and electronics authoring; 15.M08/15.T07.** Execute the actual B42/B43 native sequence, including layout repair, local model choice, offscreen triggering, geometry release, source edit and offline/hosted reopen. Preserve the independent expected nets/events and export evidence, measured aggregate budgets and accessible model/diagnostic controls. Retain this workflow in the completion summary; stage 15a's physical substitution evidence cannot be claimed here.

## Worked contract example

- [ ] **15.X01.** Populate evidence from actual named native/backend/transport replays and measured thresholds. Booleans/checkmarks produced by this example are not proof; retain reproducible inputs, outputs, screenshots where needed, timings and failure cases before changing stage status. Use this standalone illustrative acceptance example to refine the actual production API and regression; it is not an already implemented Lince interface or sufficient milestone evidence.

  ```rust
  struct WorkflowEvidence {
      replay_passed: bool,
      native_input_passed: bool,
      recovery_passed: bool,
      budgets_measured: bool,
      blockers: usize,
  }

  fn may_advance(evidence: &WorkflowEvidence) -> bool {
      evidence.replay_passed
          && evidence.native_input_passed
          && evidence.recovery_passed
          && evidence.budgets_measured
          && evidence.blockers == 0
  }

  fn main() {
      let pending = WorkflowEvidence {
          replay_passed: false,
          native_input_passed: false,
          recovery_passed: false,
          budgets_measured: false,
          blockers: 0,
      };
      assert!(!may_advance(&pending));
  }
  ```

## Architecture and task requirements

### The intended system and the first useful result

- [ ] **R0002.** **Delivery boundary revised for dependency-driven work, 2026-11-01.** Core acceptance still proves the complete useful local/offline/hosted workspace. Independent branches, including named numerical slices, may be implemented after their actual provider exports are verified and their scope authorized; a global stage-number barrier is not a technical dependency. Existing Areas, gravity, motion cooling and support remain regression obligations. Motion cooling is not temperature. Product claims require the actual relevant branch or composed gate, not an unimplemented future adapter.

- [ ] **R0003.** Before [stage 15](Core-acceptance-contracts.lingua), imported material/behavior definitions can be preserved, referenced, deduplicated and disclosed under existing rights; native tools can edit appearance, names and supported geometry. Stage 07 also delivers bounded functional behavior and stage 11a electronic authoring/design checks through these contracts. These actions do not resolve missing physical properties, predict heat or instantiate a new physical solver. Geometry validation, CAD constraint solving, meshing/simplification, bounded Walk support queries and safe replacement of existing support/colliders are core modeling/navigation work. Their mathematical algorithms do not imply an accurate material/physical simulation. Keep only the shared contract fields exercised by a core fixture; detailed future science sections preserve requirements without requiring their implementation, dataset selection, worker installation or runtime allocation early.

### Confirmed intent and context recovery

- [ ] **R0028.** **C17 — Stabilize each consumed contract before extension.** Core authoring does not require numerical material/thermal/rigid/microscopic features. Numerical branches use the verified shared model/runtime plus their declared domain prerequisites, with isolated resource/reference proofs. Core acceptance remains required for a complete core product claim; neither side advertises another branch's unfinished capability.

### Proposed defaults for refinement

- [ ] **R0052.** Delivery order is the explicit dependency graph, not the former 01–21 list. Baseline and shared interfaces are delivered once; independent consumers branch from verified exports, and composed acceptance joins their evidence. The latest owner request replaces the earlier serial priority rule. Implementation authorization and domain verification remain separate requirements.

### Owned fixture specifications

- [ ] **R0725.** The canonical fixture specifications retain full eventual proof obligations; use the ownership links in [Workspace development](../Workspace-Development.lingua#fixture-ownership) and the current declared subset. Core stages [01](Baseline-evidence.lingua)–[15](Core-acceptance-contracts.lingua) and deferred stage [15a](Circuit-and-transition-contracts.lingua) and stages [16](Material-property-contracts.lingua)–[21](Specialist-science-contracts.lingua) retain separate completion obligations. A B-number reference in an early stage selects only its stated core subset; it never requires the entire future scientific fixture. No scientific dataset/solver needs to be acquired merely to finish [stage 01](Baseline-evidence.lingua) or a hosted visit.

### Fixture phases and the stabilization boundary

- [ ] **R0766.** B01–B06, B10, B13–B15, B19/B20, B22–B36, B38/B40 — **Core proof through [stage 15](Core-acceptance-contracts.lingua):** Their stage-specific identity/geometry/query/operation/hosting subsets, with no new physical solver. B10 assembly mates are geometric; B13 addresses do not require N-body dynamics. Existing Sand/Area/support behavior remains a core regression. — **Deferred proof in stage [15a](Circuit-and-transition-contracts.lingua) and stages [16](Material-property-contracts.lingua)–[21](Specialist-science-contracts.lingua):** Only later physical/material/solver claims appended to these fixtures, such as mass-derived consequences, physically evolving assemblies or scientific worker failures B42/B43 add functional devices and electronic authoring; B44 begins numerical circuit proof in stage 15a. B41 adds the stage-specific core articulated/appearance/anatomical-inspection workflow under the same phase rule; later dynamics/biomechanics/capture cannot be counted from core posing.

- [ ] **R0774.** No row can mark a deferred fixture complete from its core metadata subset. The [stage 15](Core-acceptance-contracts.lingua) evidence matrix identifies the actual completed subset and remaining tail explicitly; all affected core/hosting/operational intentions continue as regressions when science is introduced.

### Verification obligations

- [ ] **R0813.** **Phase rule.** Apply these checks to delivered capabilities, using the stage subset requirements and [fixture ownership](../Workspace-Development.lingua#fixture-ownership). Stages [01](Baseline-evidence.lingua)–[15](Core-acceptance-contracts.lingua) verify existing physics integration and actual geometry/streaming/hosting/functional devices/electronic authoring/operations. They do not implement or pass new constitutive laws, heating, numerical experiments or multiple scientific domains. The retained scientific requirements below become gates only with stage [15a](Circuit-and-transition-contracts.lingua) and stages [16](Material-property-contracts.lingua)–[21](Specialist-science-contracts.lingua); early profiling uses real core work, not a placeholder physics benchmark.

### Confirmed owner decisions, 2026-10-18, 2026-10-20 and 2026-10-21

- [ ] **R0848.** **Q21 — Stabilize before additional physical simulation.** stages [01](Baseline-evidence.lingua)–[15](Core-acceptance-contracts.lingua) deliver and stabilize workspace/scale/modeling/hosting/operational capabilities and existing Areas, gravity and motion cooling. Stage [15a](Circuit-and-transition-contracts.lingua) and stages [16](Material-property-contracts.lingua)–[21](Specialist-science-contracts.lingua) retain all new physical-material evaluation/derivation, heating/thermal behavior, further rigid/flexible/joint physics, laboratory experiments, optional calculated-state recording and accurate specialist simulation as explicitly deferred final stages. Passive definitions/appearance and geometry/navigation are not physical accuracy. Earlier scope, fixtures or descriptive sections cannot override this order.

## Workflow, correctness and performance evidence

- [ ] Instantiate the local **15.W** acceptance rows before their implementation: pin the real fixture/profile, applicable hard assertions/numeric limits, quality rubric and unit/integration/fault/native/performance evidence. Apply the existing owned requirements as well as the matrix. Record each relevant previously verified workflow exercised in composition and any temporary regression/repair; measure through actual services rather than counting checked tasks.

- [ ] **Real workload.** Replay the actual personal-place and shared-workspace stories while operational queries and a structure edit remain usable. Increase real indexed/instanced content within the frozen dataset/profile and prove select/edit/save/revisit/recover actions under the cap; passing a 30,000-square renderer test alone cannot advance this gate.

- [ ] **R0571.** **[stage 15](Core-acceptance-contracts.lingua) — L0–L5 core stabilization** — **Intention and defined deliverable:** Resolve core regressions and prove a useful offline/local/hosted modeling workspace independently of the numerical branches — **Correctness/failure evidence and performance obligation:** Replay stage-specific B01–B40 core subsets below, appearance/input review and mixed workloads on named hardware. Verify old Areas/gravity/motion cooling, precision/identity/undo, partial/offline closure, native permissions, guest/Organ isolation, recovery and measured budget/resource release. No missing deferred material/thermal/physics feature blocks this gate, and no stub counts as delivered. Include B41 core acceptance and its body/camera/appearance/anatomy demand isolation under the same mixed-workload limits.

- [ ] Run the actual native/backend/persistence/transport path for every 15.M milestone, including the supported failure and permission cases. Retain fixture/input revisions, command receipts/output identity and a reproducible run recipe; inspect native appearance/focus/input where relevant. A standalone example, empty adapter/UI, helper test or synthetic draw-count benchmark cannot complete a workflow.

- [ ] Record named hardware/build/profile/source rights, cold/warm/offline conditions, visible input/commit/frame percentiles, applicable query/job/error results, CPU/GPU/disk/transfer/queue/staging peaks and last-demand release. Apply the stage's agreed limits, including transient old/new products; resolve failures or document a specifically owner-reviewed measured profile change before claiming success.

- [ ] Run only checks justified by the changed contracts through repository cargo xtask/Nix workflows and `cargo check` with warnings as errors. If a schema change is required, append a new migration/checksum and run the store check/migration guards; never rewrite an old migration. Keep old web code and unrelated changes untouched.

- [ ] **Integrated software evidence.** Extend the existing mixed-workload replay with real native/Fiote result editing and linked-work reconciliation, reporting model-provider response delay separately from native feedback. Confirm existing flat/manual/offline use remains complete with the provider unavailable and no additional devices configured. Include B42/B43 functional devices/electronic authoring, preserve earlier scale, hosting, security and resource targets, without requiring every numerical branch to be built or to remain unbuilt. Independently delivered numerical capabilities retain their own evidence.

## Advance gate

- [ ] Verify every local **15.W** contract and required milestone with both hard assertions/measurements and recorded qualitative review. Confirm all required earlier capabilities still hold using current affected proofs and retained unchanged evidence; close recorded regressions at their owning stages before advancement. Optional examples and deferred calculations remain explicitly scoped, and no required workflow can disappear during summary compression.

- [ ] **R0675.** The intended local/offline/hosted workspace is usable and measured, with no unresolved blocker in its claimed core scope and no dependence on new material/thermal/scientific execution. This closes core product acceptance. Each numerical package may independently begin after its named provider exports are verified and its implementation scope is authorized. Unbuilt numerical requirements stay pending; numerical capabilities already delivered retain their own evidence. Core stabilization neither completes nor removes those requirements.

- [ ] Mark this contract acceptance complete only when every required milestone, workflow, task contribution and applicable native/failure/resource proof below passes. Independent consumers may already use a verified package export; they do not borrow this still-pending whole-contract completion.

- [ ] Request owner review of the concrete workflow/evidence where implementation approval or a changed scope/budget is needed; reuse approval already present. Do not replace missing behavior with weaker acceptance wording or silently pull deferred science into a core milestone.

## Completion summary

- [ ] Keep this handoff factual throughout implementation: record verified slices and evidence while the stage remains pending/in progress, retaining full detail for unfinished scope. After the gate passes, finalize one or two short paragraphs describing what was implemented, actual module/interface ownership and why; include a consequential rejected alternative briefly when useful. Add a distinct compact paragraph for every **15.W** workflow, preserving original milestone IDs, built-in versus recipe scope, required behavior, hard bounds, qualitative criteria and evidence links. Update this contract's acceptance status and its contributing package handoffs only with verified evidence; a regression changes current verification to `Repair required` until repaired.

  ```yaml
  status: pending
  gate_verified_against_revision: pending
  implementation_and_rationale: pending
  relevant_alternatives_not_chosen: []
  retained_workflow_contracts: []
  delivered_user_workflows: []
  contract_and_module_changes: []
  fixtures_and_replay_commands: []
  observed_error_latency_and_resource_results: []
  qualitative_review_results: []
  permission_failure_and_recovery_evidence: []
  remaining_blocked_or_deferred_scope: []
  current_regressions_and_repair_state: []
  next_stage_context: []
  ```

- [ ] After verified implementation, remove only completed task detail as required by repository planning rules; preserve this factual completion summary, unfinished requirements and usable links to the implemented contracts/evidence. Do not replace a pending task with an invented success summary. Keep the retained workflow paragraphs independently readable; replace completed instructions/examples with real contract/test links and redirect incoming anchors before pruning detail. Unfinished scope keeps its full implementation context.
